WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.535
Oliver was the ring bearer at a wedding.

2
00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:08.123
His job was to carry the rings.

3
00:00:08.124 --> 00:00:12.077
The wedding was starting soon.

4
00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:16.227
"This suit is too tight," Oliver said.

5
00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:19.399
"I don't like this bow tie."

6
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.500
"But you look so cute!" Mom said.

7
00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:30.242
"Why must I carry this pillow?" Oliver asked.

8
00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:34.108
"That's what ring bearers do," Harry said.

9
00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:38.208
"They carry the wedding rings on a pillow."

10
00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:42.141
"It's an important job," Dad said.

11
00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:48.050
"I wish I wasn't in this wedding," Oliver said.

12
00:00:48.051 --> 00:00:52.308
Emmy watched the photographer take pictures.

13
00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:57.606
The bridesmaids wore long dresses and carried pink flowers.

14
00:00:57.607 --> 00:01:02.473
"Their dresses are so pretty," she said.

15
00:01:02.474 --> 00:01:05.626
"I wish I was in this wedding."

16
00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:09.453
Suddenly the photographer bumped into Oliver.

17
00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:12.077
Oliver dropped his pillow.

18
00:01:12.078 --> 00:01:21.244
The bride and groom's rings rolled away.

19
00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:26.544
"Where are the rings?" Mom asked.

20
00:01:26.545 --> 00:01:31.664
"I don't know!" Oliver cried.

21
00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:34.904
The Carters looked everywhere.

22
00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:41.279
But they couldn't find the rings.

23
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.802
"You're in trouble now," Harry said to Oliver.

24
00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:50.951
"I'm glad I'm not in this wedding!" Emmy said.

25
00:01:50.952 --> 00:01:54.255
Oliver ran over to the bride.

26
00:01:54.256 --> 00:01:58.781
"I can't be your ring bearer anymore," he said.

27
00:01:58.782 --> 00:02:04.004
"I lost the rings!"

28
00:02:04.005 --> 00:02:07.977
"Don't worry, Oliver," the bride said.

29
00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:13.691
"The best man is holding the real rings."

30
00:02:13.692 --> 00:02:16.447
She smiled.

31
00:02:16.448 --> 00:02:29.511
"So you can still be in our wedding!"

